# K03-EXPLICIT-RECEIVER-FRAMES (the author, 2026-10-06: `b: merge: A C` or `b: merge(A C)`; `b: merge A C` is a
# typo): an application with arguments is its Frame, whatever the receiver.  In a method: merge's short, compact
# and completed vertical spellings with one operand and with two, each result its own copy; a merge nested in a
# condition's body; merge's Frame returned from a factory, short and compact; and another receiver's Frames,
# `length: arr` and `length(arr)`.  The vertical spelling translates as the short one does, byte for byte.
# Entry 7.
Model:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Model
Extra:
    size_t: z 2U
end: Extra
fn: add () int
    return: 4
end: add
fn: make () fn: () int
    return: merge: add
end: make
fn: make2 () fn: () int
    return: merge(add)
end: make2
fn: rdx (Model: m) size_t
    return: m\x
end: rdx
fn: check () int
    []: int arr 3
    size_t: n 0U
    size_t: k 0U
    a: merge: Model
    b: merge(Model)
    c:
        merge:
            Model
    ---
    d: merge: Model Extra
    e: merge(Model Extra)
    a\x: 5U
    if: b\x != 1U || c\x != 1U || d\x != 1U || d\z != 2U || e\z != 2U || Model\x != 1U
        return: 81
    if: a\x = 5U
        f: merge: d
        f\z: 9U
        if: f\x != 1U || d\z != 2U || f\z != 9U
            return: 82
    ---
    if: rdx(a) != 5U
        return: 83
    n: length: arr
    k: length(arr)
    if: n != 3U || k != 3U
        return: 84
    @: w make()
    @: v make2()
    if: w() + v() != 8
        return: 85
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
